  i The template ref root is created with ref().
  
    10 │ import { ref, shallowRef } from "vue";
    11 │ 
  > 12 │ const root = ref();
       │       ^^^^
    13 │ const heading = ref(null);
    14 │ const link = shallowRef();
  
  i Vue links this variable to the element only by its name, so renaming the variable breaks the link without warning.
  
  i Use useTemplateRef("root") instead, which names the element explicitly.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

